\begin{proposition}
\label{prop:2.2}
 Let \( (X, d) \) be a metric space, and let \( (E, d|_{E \times E}) \) be a subspace of \( (X, d) \). Let \( \iota_{E \to X} : E \to X \) be the inclusion map, defined by setting \( \iota_{E \to X}(x) := x \) for all \( x \in E \). Show that \( \iota_{E \to X} \) is continuous.
\end{proposition}

proof:
\begin{proof}
\label{prf:prop:2.2}
Fix $x\in E$ and $\varepsilon>0$. Choose $\delta:=\varepsilon$. If $y\in E$ satisfies $d_E(x,y)<\delta$, then by definition of $d_E$ one has $d(\iota_{E\to X}(x),\iota_{E\to X}(y))=d(x,y)=d_E(x,y)<\varepsilon$. This verifies continuity of $\iota_{E\to X}$ at $x$. Since $x\in E$ was arbitrary, $\iota_{E\to X}$ is continuous on $E$.
\end{proof}

